---
description: Secure coding rules for all code
alwaysApply: true
---
- Follow the OWASP Top 10. Flag any code that could fall into one of its categories.
- Use parameterized queries. Never build SQL or shell commands by joining strings with input.
- Validate all external input at the boundary.
- Never hard-code secrets, keys or passwords. Read them from the environment or a secrets manager.
- Never log full card numbers, account numbers or personal data. Mask card numbers to the last four digits.
- Use the secrets module for tokens, never random.
- Check authorization before any action on an account.
- Don't add a dependency without saying why, and pin its version.